From 1786325e48554fef877f51467403dcfbab9b9cf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan McQuillan <ryan@appliedaisystems.io>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 00:32:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Fix dropped sync wakes: coalesce mid-cycle wakes into one
 follow-up cycle

A sharedWorkspaceChanged/orgWorkspaceChanged wake arriving while a sync cycle
was in flight hit the bare 'running' guard and was silently discarded - no
queue, no re-arm - so the receiver fell back to the 20s interval. Cycles run
long in proportion to dirty-row count (serial PUTs), so on an active shared
desk two peers each drop the other's wakes and collaboration lags 7-8s.

The fix records the wake and runs exactly one coalesced follow-up cycle from
the finally: N wakes during a cycle collapse into one re-run; wakes during the
re-run coalesce into the next; quiet input converges immediately. No timers,
no transport changes; enabled/token setDisabled semantics preserved. The
coalescer is a dependency-free module with a 6-test behavioural pin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
